In particular, the largest challenge was the construction of a part-of-speech tagger and we base our work on two main systems that have been developed based on annotated corpora. Firstly, we look at the system of U´ı Dhonnchadha and van Genabith (2006), which was developed on a general language domain and secondly we refer to the system of Lynn et al. (2015), which was developed speciﬁcally for tweets. We then looked at an alternative approach using the terminology database, Tearma1, to provide an annotation over the Irish Wikipedia, ‘An Vicipe´id’2. For both the systems trained on part-of-speech corpora and those on the terminology database, we compare them for the challenge of recognizing terms. We show how we incorporate into our term recognition system morphology information extracted from Pota Focal (Meˇchura, 2018). To analyse this we developed a small gold standard dataset of Wikipedia articles and compared the two methods on this dataset3. We then describe the construction of the automatic
